/* book Worked example: Q: A 230 V, 50 Hz supply feeds a 50 Ω resistor through a single-phase PWM AC chopper switching at 10 kHz with D = 0.6 and no output filter. Find ton, Vo, the power, V1 and its share of the power, the lowest sideband, and the supply power factor without and with an ideal input filter.
   1. T = 1/10 000 = 100 µs, so ton = 0.6 × 100 = 60 µs.
   2. Vo = 230 × √0.6 = 230 × 0.7746 = 178.2 V. P = 178.2²/50 = 634.8 W.
   3. V1 = 0.6 × 230 = 138.0 V. Its power is 138.0²/50 = 380.9 W; the other 253.9 W is carried by the sidebands.
   4. Lowest unwanted frequency: fsw − f = 10 000 − 50 = 9950 Hz, the 199th harmonic of 50 Hz.
   5. No filter: supply current RMS = 178.2/50 = 3.564 A, so PF = 634.8/(230 × 3.564) = 0.775 = √0.6.
   6. Ideal filter: the supply gives only the 50 Hz average, 138.0/50 = 2.76 A, in phase. Check: 230 × 2.76 = 634.8 W. PF = 1.
   Answer: ton = 60 µs, Vo = 178.2 V, P = 634.8 W, V1 = 138.0 V carrying 380.9 W, lowest sideband 9950 Hz, power factor 0.775 without a filter and close to 1 with one. */
